    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\n```\ncdef IntOrFloat f(IntOrFloat x) except -1:\n                                        ^\n------------------------------------------------------------\nfusedreturn.pyx:5:40: Cannot coerce to a type that is not specialized\n```\n\nThis should work because `-1` would be a valid exception value for both `int` or `float`\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n```cython\ncdef fused IntOrFloat:\n    int\n    float\n\ncdef IntOrFloat f(IntOrFloat x) except -1:\n    return x\n```\n\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\n_No response_\n\n### OS\n\nLinux\n\n### Python version\n\n3.13\n\n### Cython version\n\nCurrent master\n\n### Additional context\n\nPossibly worth checking if https://github.com/cython/cython/pull/5737 solves it/helps... It certainly contains a test that looks similar",
